          "type": "definition",
          "text": "Triangle ABC is right-angled at B, where A and C are two complementary acute angles; the side opposite angle C is called the opposite leg, the side adjacent to angle C is called the adjacent, and the side opposite the right angle is called the hypotenuse.",
          "page": 50
        },
        {
